  "_key": "!scenes!cf17d2b939a9b756",
  "description": "<p>The Amber Gel facility. Barely used by the Hive and showing only general activity at the loading dock — trucks from Strice Foods load each morning, and the drums are already waiting for them. The only person the truckers ever see is <strong>Craft</strong>.</p><p>Lighting is whatever filters through the high green-tinted windows; the power is on, so the runners can switch the fluorescents on if they want. <strong>The stairway is unlit.</strong></p><p><strong>None of the doors are locked</strong> and all are easily operable. The freight elevator is conventional and fully operational, though its control panel shows physical damage.</p><p><strong>Rooms:</strong> Main area with disused conventional food-production equipment (dusty, poorly maintained), loading dock, freight elevator, small group of empty abandoned offices, stairway up to the roof and down to the Lower Level.</p><p><em>Layout derived from the printed floorplan on Queen Euphoria p.44. Measured 24 × 14 m by 1 m = 85.5 px on a 300 dpi render of p.44 (PDF 46); the printed 1 m floor tiles line up with a metre grid laid over it, 24 x 12 m building plus the loading dock outside the double doors — the map carries a \"□ = 1 metre\" legend, so the scale is the book's, not an estimate.</em></p>"
}
